        "html": "<p><b>Fishbourne Palace</b></p><p><b>Construction</b></p><ul><li>The first buildings on the site contained food for the [[7]]</li><li>The palace building surrounded [[8]]</li><li>In the 2nd and 3rd centuries colour was added to the [[9]] of the palace.</li></ul><p><b>Discovery</b></p><ul><li>The first part of the palace to be found was part of a [[10]]</li></ul><p><b>Possible inhabitants</b></p><ul><li>Cogidubnus – he is named in several writings</li><li>Sallustius Lucullus – he may have lived there until approximately [[11]] AD</li><li>Verica – a British king</li><li>Catuarus – his [[12]] was found here</li></ul><p><b>Present Day</b></p><ul><li>A [[13]] has been built on the site to help protect it.</li></ul>"
