        "html": "<p><b>Provine's early findings on yawns</b></p><p>Through his observation of yawns, Provine was able to confirm that [[27]] do not exist. Just like a [[28]], yawns cannot be interrupted after they have begun. This is because yawns occur as a [[29]] rather than a stimulus response as was previously thought. In measuring the time taken to yawn, Provine found that a typical yawn lasts about [[30]]. He also found that it is common for people to yawn a number of times in quick succession with the yawns usually being around [[31]] apart. When studying whether length and rate were connected, Provine concluded that people who yawn less do not necessarily produce [[32]] to make up for this.</p>"
